  "novel": "Ted became a [[third wheel|third wheel]] on Barney's double date. He felt [[awkward|awkward]] and [[excluded|exclude]], watching Barney charm both women with [[ease|ease]].\n\nMeanwhile, Marshall [[obsessed|obsess]] over a [[stain|stain]] on the floor. He [[scrubbed|scrub]] for hours, but the mark refused to [[fade|fade]]. \"It's [[ruining|ruin]] my life,\" he [[declared|declare]].\n\nRobin and Gael hit a [[bump|bump]]. His [[carefree|carefree]] attitude began to [[annoy|annoy]] her. She [[craved|crave]] structure; he [[preferred|prefer]] [[spontaneity|spontaneity]].\n\nAt the bar, Ted [[seized|seize]] his moment. He [[approached|approach]] a woman and [[blurted|blurt]] out a greeting. She smiled. The third wheel [[syndrome|syndrome]], he discovered, was curable — if you had courage to start participating.",
